// REJECTS: Column data type INTEGER does not expect any parameters
//
// The other direction of the same walker check: INTEGER, BIGINT, DATE, TIMESTAMP, FLOAT and
// friends take NO parameters, and `INTEGER(10)` is refused even though the grammar's shared
// column rule happily matches it.
//
// `INT(10)` is valid DDL in several dialects, so this is a construct a user can plausibly
// write and a rewrite can plausibly accept. Both halves of the arity rule are pinned
// because a rewrite that implements one and not the other looks correct on every fixture
// that exercises the other.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::IntWidth
(
   Table T (ID INTEGER(10) PRIMARY KEY)
)
